==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/auːr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|auːr|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ár|lang=non}}. Cognates include: Gothic {{term|𐌰𐌹𐍂||tr=air|early|lang=got}}, Old English {{term|ar|ār|lang=ang}} and {{term|ærlice|lang=ang}} (English {{term|early|lang=en}}).<ref name="torp">Alf Torp, "Nynorsk Etymologisk Ordbok", Oslo 1992 (reprint), ISBN 82-90520-17-4; ''aarlege'', ''aar''</ref>

====Adverb====
{{is-adv}}

# {{rare|lang=is}} [[early]]

=====Derived terms=====
* [[ár og síð]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ár||year|lang=non}}. Cognates include: Dutch and Afrikaans {{term|jaar|lang=nl}}, English {{term|year|lang=en}}, German {{term|Jahr|lang=de}}, Danish, Norwegian and Swedish {{term|år|lang=da}}.<ref name="torp"/>

====Noun====
{{is-noun|n|árs|ár}}

# [[year]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-n-s||á|r}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|árlegur}}
* {{l|is|ártíð}}
* {{l|is|í ár}}
* {{l|is|gleðilegt nýtt ár}}
* {{l|is|gleðilegt ár}}
* {{l|is|hlaupaár}}
* {{l|is|áramót}}
* {{l|is|nýár}}

===Etymology 3===
Inflection of [[ár#Icelandic|ár]] ("year")  <!-- same etymology as above; could be integrated -->

====Noun====
'''ár''' {{n}}

# {{is-inflection of|ár|indef|acc|s}}
# {{plural of|[[ár]]|lang=is}}
# {{is-inflection of|ár|indef|acc|p}}

===Etymology 4===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ár|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Germanic|airō|lang=is}}. Cognates include: Old English {{term|ar|ār|oar|lang=ang}} (English {{term|oar|lang=en}}).<ref name="torp"/>

====Noun====
{{is-noun|f|árar|árar}}

# [[oar]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-f-s1||á|r}}

=====Derived terms=====
* [[árinni kennir illur ræðari]]
* [[árabátur]]
