==Irish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sga|ga}} {{term|ar|lang=sga}} < {{proto|Celtic|anserom|lang=ga}} < {{proto|Indo-European|n̥serōm|lang=ga}} < *''nes-'' (“we, us”); compare German {{term|unser||lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=ga|[ɑːɾˠ]|[əɾˠ]|[ə]}}

===Pronoun===
{{infl|ga|pronoun|possessive}}

# [[our]]

====Usage notes====
Triggers eclipsis on the following word:
* '''''ár''' [[teach|dteach]]'' – our house
* [[athair|Ár nAthair]] – [[Our Father]]

